      <div type="clause" n="30.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 30.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="332" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.7"/> se að þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.8"/> forðcume, ceose se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.9"/> man, þe þær betihtled<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.10"/> syg, swæðer he wylle, swa anfeald ordal<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.2-2"/> swa pundes weorðne að innan þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þrim<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.11"/> hundredan, ofer XXX peninga.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.12"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="332" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf se að ðonne forðcume, ceose se man, ðe ðær betyhtlod sy, swa hwæðer swa he wylle, swa anfeald ordal swa pundes wurðne að innan ðrim hundrede<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.2"/>, ofer XXX peninga.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="332" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif se að þonne forðcume, ceose se man, þe þær betihtlad sy, swa weðer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.1"/> he wylle, swa anfeald ordal swa pundes weor[þ]ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.2-3"/> að innan þam þrym hundredan, ofer þritti pænega.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="30.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="333" ed="#liebermann"/>Si iuramentum procedat, eligat accusatus alterutrum quod uelit, siue simplex ordalium siue iuramentum unius librę in tribus hundretis, super XXX denarios.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="30.2" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="333" ed="#liebermann"/>Si sacramentum bene processerit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.3"/>, ille calumniatus eligat, quid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.4"/> horum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.5"/> uoluerit, aut simplex iudicium<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.6"/> aut sacramentum XX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.star"/> solidorum in tribus hundredis, ultra XXXta denarios.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="30.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="333" ed="#liebermann"/>Si ergo illud iuramentum perfectum fuerit, eligat tunc calumpniatus utrum maluerit, siue simplex Dei iudicium siue libram ualens iuramentum de tribus centenariis, supra triginta denarios.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="30.2" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="190" ed="#robertson"/>Gyf se að ðonne forðcume, ceose se man ðe ðær betyhtlod sy swa hwæðer swa<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_30-2.robnote.fn.3"/> he wylle, swa anfeald ordal swa pundes wurðne að innan ðrim hundrede, ofer XXX peninga.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="270" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gyf se að þonne forðcume, ceose se man þe þær betihtled syg swæðer he wylle: swa anfeald ordal swa pundes weorðne að innan þam þrim hundredan ofer XXX peninga.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="332" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn nun dieser Eid zu Stande kommt, dann wähle jener Mann, welcher da beschuldigt ist, eines von beiden [Reinigungsmitteln] wie er will: entweder einfaches Ordal oder einen Eid von 1 Pfund [Silbers<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_30-2.lnote.de.1"/>] Werth, [mit Helfern] nicht weiter her als aus drei [dieser und zwei Nachbar-] Hundertschaften: [bei einem Object] über 30 Pfennig.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If this oath then succeeds, let the man who is accused choose whichever of the two [means of clearing himself] he wishes: either the single ordeal or an oath worth 1 pound [of silver], [with helpers] from no further away than three hundreds [this one and two neighbouring ones]: [for an object] over 30 pence.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_30-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="191" ed="#robertson"/>If the oath is forthcoming, the man who is accused there shall choose whichever he will—either the simple ordeal or an oath equivalent to a pound in value, [supported by compurgators found] within the three hundreds, [in the case of an object] over 30 pence in value.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="466" ed="#whitelock"/>And if the oath is then forthcoming, the man who is there accused is to choose which he will have, whether simple ordeal or an oath worth a pound within the three hundreds, in a case of [stolen goods of] over 30 pence.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="271" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Then, if the oath taking will proceed, the person who is accused shall there select whichever he prefers: a simple ordeal or an oath valued at one pound supported by witnesses from within the three hundreds in disputes involving property valued at more than thirty pence.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="332"><ref target="clause:IAtr_1-3">I Atr 1.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. I Atr. 1, 3</note>
        <note type="editorial">A's ‘weor[þ]ne’ corrected by Liebermann (MS ‘weorne’). Liebermann compares I Atr 1.3.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 333, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðone <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðone Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-lad sy, swa hwæþer he wille <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-lad sy, swa hwæþer he wille Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-le <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-le Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðrym <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðrym Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">penega <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">penega Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">332</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">weorne <hi rend="italic">A</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">weorne A</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Cb;</hi> prec. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Cb; prec. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quod <hi rend="italic">Db</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quod Db</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eorum <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eorum Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ordalium <hi rend="italic">S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ordalium S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">333</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. I Cn.</hi> 3, 2 <hi rend="italic">Hs. Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. I Cn. 3, 2 MS Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_30-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Inst rechnet wie 13, 2⁴ das Pfund zu 20 Normann. Schillingen.—Dieser Eid ist leichter als der <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 22⁴ geforderte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Inst, as in 13, 2⁴, reckons the pound at 20 Norman shillings.—This oath is easier than that required <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 22⁴</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_30-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With this clause and the one following, cf. I Atr. 1, 3 f.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_30-2.robnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">190</biblScope></bibl><label>swa</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">swæðer he</hi> G, Ld; <hi rend="italic">swa weðer he</hi> A.</seg></note>
